{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:36:30Z","created_by_operation":"op_42d951e5c8e3444c995397f51bca083f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_02a67e5fbd8668710ef87e77d6a7f37949cf8271012baeaaa6a29ba1a0cc7255","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"respeak-io/episko@974192b540db snapshot 4ce3ea1d5573290e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_6302e04c66335cb7455fe0e748c18734c5425be52c505b9eecb07f97f7531cc2"],"source_ids":["src_074816f558215de0a5e8986c98cdcc40"],"text":"Task discovery never executes the project: just --dump, task --list and mise tasks ls sit behind a trust gate, Makefiles are parsed statically, and tasks that cannot run are shown greyed with the reason rather than hidden.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:36:30Z","updated_by_operation":"op_42d951e5c8e3444c995397f51bca083f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:36:30Z","created_by_operation":"op_42d951e5c8e3444c995397f51bca083f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_2dcc3989d0b6b40663e797f5005a2a58a72f5c14f8a00c44668b7b263e68a213","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"respeak-io/episko@974192b540db snapshot 4ce3ea1d5573290e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_44263469b7f1573b6f9102cbec2b75435175ce455147a3742d636af39f3a4445"],"source_ids":["src_074816f558215de0a5e8986c98cdcc40"],"text":"Episko gives each coding-agent session its own real terminal; Claude Code and Codex are first-class integrated providers, while other installed CLIs work through a terminal-only adapter pane.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:36:30Z","updated_by_operation":"op_42d951e5c8e3444c995397f51bca083f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:36:30Z","created_by_operation":"op_42d951e5c8e3444c995397f51bca083f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_308719839b799042f0d33499aa4b79f1fcaa4c07a263ae45f87f5b02c9a32039","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"respeak-io/episko@974192b540db snapshot 4ce3ea1d5573290e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_369f89eacc7d9dafc5f06bc4125cef50997f6b9b08b1edd1cab9c5b7d27e5163","slc_9b2d159e8168cef1bbfba60d7eba085b65ad86dd0c897ebf6b9d2926611c2628"],"source_ids":["src_074816f558215de0a5e8986c98cdcc40"],"text":"Release builds target Apple-silicon macOS and Windows x64; Intel Macs are not covered and Linux is not packaged. The macOS build is self-signed but not notarized, so Gatekeeper quarantines the download and users must clear the quarantine flag before opening.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:36:30Z","updated_by_operation":"op_42d951e5c8e3444c995397f51bca083f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:36:30Z","created_by_operation":"op_42d951e5c8e3444c995397f51bca083f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3fc01ec2cf3f6d16e7e7d84b6c7883a00215834cb8cdad4775c380061ee79393","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"respeak-io/episko@974192b540db snapshot 4ce3ea1d5573290e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_80ef9988802e8a6e5892d9d1ec830fbdd933a8ca2cf31dd3508c498ca7b90933","slc_9c4c1bea01026a2293c16dc7b34ecc28318fef03c6a887b4ab27b75dacb2d648"],"source_ids":["src_074816f558215de0a5e8986c98cdcc40"],"text":"The app discovers and runs tasks the project already ships — .episko/tasks.toml, .vscode/tasks.json and launch.json, package.json scripts, justfile, Taskfile.yml, mise.toml, Makefile, Cargo.toml — in the same PTY panes as agent sessions.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:36:30Z","updated_by_operation":"op_42d951e5c8e3444c995397f51bca083f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:36:30Z","created_by_operation":"op_42d951e5c8e3444c995397f51bca083f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_5166c510d594cfebe5ac17cd5ea67ddfbf4a3f819e189c51f5806b84a072ea55","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"respeak-io/episko@974192b540db snapshot 4ce3ea1d5573290e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_a042382aed963ef1aeffdc986f1f730501e68543f3aac88fbef0d4ba1f306bed"],"source_ids":["src_074816f558215de0a5e8986c98cdcc40"],"text":"Building from source requires Node.js 18+, pnpm, stable Rust with Tauri system dependencies, and at least one supported coding-agent CLI on PATH.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:36:30Z","updated_by_operation":"op_42d951e5c8e3444c995397f51bca083f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:36:30Z","created_by_operation":"op_42d951e5c8e3444c995397f51bca083f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_58d49cb0f4bbf07aa2f5bbceb66c3bb570d386c58df373e7437011bad4b2d702","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"respeak-io/episko@974192b540db snapshot 4ce3ea1d5573290e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_f772959393d6d131f590e167a39fd0675cf472e6fe8122deadfbfe3bd8a0e971"],"source_ids":["src_074816f558215de0a5e8986c98cdcc40"],"text":"Telemetry POSTs are tagged with a launch id so events route to the correct pane, and routing survives /clear, /compact and /resume, each of which makes Claude mint a new runtime session_id; the permission hook is a blocking call held open until answered.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:36:30Z","updated_by_operation":"op_42d951e5c8e3444c995397f51bca083f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:36:30Z","created_by_operation":"op_42d951e5c8e3444c995397f51bca083f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_5fdb4a55b5f93b8e54ab4685d3897a0a1f243dcb65affd7316d34188af16d0ca","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"respeak-io/episko@974192b540db snapshot 4ce3ea1d5573290e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_d81fec555331ff11678c41fdc26c05a6d7824f7c7929414a1ca35e0d34869f3c"],"source_ids":["src_074816f558215de0a5e8986c98cdcc40"],"text":"When Claude or Codex requests to run something, the app surfaces the command with a risk read and lets the user allow, deny, or hand it to the terminal; starting permission/sandbox policy is stored per integrated agent.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:36:30Z","updated_by_operation":"op_42d951e5c8e3444c995397f51bca083f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:36:30Z","created_by_operation":"op_42d951e5c8e3444c995397f51bca083f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_68b982be134a8e8f6e2c67f9ad093146411768073c38a57ca7321ec7be2855b5","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"respeak-io/episko@974192b540db snapshot 4ce3ea1d5573290e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2a7dabc68cb66e7a1d95740d0470a609c26d5e00125b164eff3c44613a9ca6e6","slc_6302e04c66335cb7455fe0e748c18734c5425be52c505b9eecb07f97f7531cc2"],"source_ids":["src_074816f558215de0a5e8986c98cdcc40"],"text":"Personal preferences go to localStorage while project facts go to .episko/tasks.toml, described as the only file the app writes, edited via toml_edit so comments and ordering survive; shared digests and notes can be committed as .episko/digest.md and .episko/notes.toml.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:36:30Z","updated_by_operation":"op_42d951e5c8e3444c995397f51bca083f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:36:30Z","created_by_operation":"op_42d951e5c8e3444c995397f51bca083f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_a6b21826e31b91d28a20606c7db0ad041f1309935f98c49d0766efa6068f5a83","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"respeak-io/episko@974192b540db snapshot 4ce3ea1d5573290e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2a7dabc68cb66e7a1d95740d0470a609c26d5e00125b164eff3c44613a9ca6e6","slc_abc41734915764b5ce3138f6bd0a791053a86bbe5a525520856575550055c7f8"],"source_ids":["src_074816f558215de0a5e8986c98cdcc40"],"text":"Each project gets a dashboard with per-day commit and session summaries, issues with triage suggestions, GitHub claims that mark an issue as taken by an agent, and worktree checkouts; feature depth degrades for plain git repos and bare folders.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:36:30Z","updated_by_operation":"op_42d951e5c8e3444c995397f51bca083f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:36:30Z","created_by_operation":"op_42d951e5c8e3444c995397f51bca083f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_e49b74051b68b59b2510320f15ea466d3feb96182df10ee601e2eb6e1d9226fe","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"respeak-io/episko@974192b540db snapshot 4ce3ea1d5573290e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_7d5e7db638f1f6f8622d411683c5b2f4ba6a59e07676b32a17d19687a3556dc1"],"source_ids":["src_074816f558215de0a5e8986c98cdcc40"],"text":"On each Claude launch the app writes a throwaway --settings file whose statusLine command and lifecycle hooks POST to a tiny_http server on an ephemeral localhost port; Codex launches use a loopback App Server, and both transports feed one provider-neutral event reducer.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:36:30Z","updated_by_operation":"op_42d951e5c8e3444c995397f51bca083f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:36:30Z","created_by_operation":"op_42d951e5c8e3444c995397f51bca083f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_ea76b3cd23d31bb7c1bd2f03431942a813d45aae3a2ed963f18ed0290a1ef2fb","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"respeak-io/episko@974192b540db snapshot 4ce3ea1d5573290e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0f26496fd72c6444e8c01dd5df8032e54f28b555ce765d745e51c643367e83e8","slc_5cb8b077b9be7dae5990c93fe75ec8b3860fa1277c932db609404a3d42401ed6"],"source_ids":["src_6760d0311ba75608abc669476b6bc308"],"text":"Repository development practice: CI runs on every push and PR to dev/main on both macOS and Windows, covering strict tsc typecheck, vitest suites (~1,535 it blocks), cargo check/test --locked (~270 #[test] functions) and clippy with -D warnings.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:36:30Z","updated_by_operation":"op_42d951e5c8e3444c995397f51bca083f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:36:30Z","created_by_operation":"op_42d951e5c8e3444c995397f51bca083f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_f0ead2dfe1eb6f65a6454b29a6307f741f7cd1533a730aa3dea386e76c6535bc","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"respeak-io/episko@974192b540db snapshot 4ce3ea1d5573290e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0a63f0b5c11ecfd3c4ae7ad7d335fdcbc18b74ee814f2191f7359901a7dee250"],"source_ids":["src_6760d0311ba75608abc669476b6bc308"],"text":"The app detects external Claude sessions started outside Episko and shows them as read-only mirrors in the sidebar, and can jump to the terminal tab or window hosting such a session.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:36:30Z","updated_by_operation":"op_42d951e5c8e3444c995397f51bca083f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:36:30Z","created_by_operation":"op_42d951e5c8e3444c995397f51bca083f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_f723a986601aab63a03fdc1f1d0673b3deb16cf23fb23408fb86a3e98396b525","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"respeak-io/episko@974192b540db snapshot 4ce3ea1d5573290e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_a49707b3f61e3d06da0cbd111d802202edbe15e5a54a03b83c14fb4507fd2a22"],"source_ids":["src_074816f558215de0a5e8986c98cdcc40"],"text":"The app is built on Tauri v2 with a Rust backend and system WebView frontend, uses portable-pty for PTYs (forkpty on macOS, ConPTY on Windows), tiny_http as a localhost telemetry receiver, and xterm.js for terminal rendering.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:36:30Z","updated_by_operation":"op_42d951e5c8e3444c995397f51bca083f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:36:30Z","created_by_operation":"op_42d951e5c8e3444c995397f51bca083f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_f91685431e1d62c25b8b3b80a97ba9903b98796c4b53200736b3eeef2492cb50","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"respeak-io/episko@974192b540db snapshot 4ce3ea1d5573290e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_83192df6117242c879a681256d1315f542ea98f506c0e6b60df0aaf9f16b1e2a","slc_9f57bf24fe854fccb376ec585c53f3139cab4019d331c48eedc8c5d1f25310ff"],"source_ids":["src_6760d0311ba75608abc669476b6bc308"],"text":"Repository development practice: ignored cargo contract tests against real Claude Code (instrumentation, permission modes, temp-dir layout) are run manually via cargo test -- --ignored because CI lacks claude on PATH; one of them spends tokens and needs authentication.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:36:30Z","updated_by_operation":"op_42d951e5c8e3444c995397f51bca083f"}
